# (build 110) The synth backend switched while the title's theme plays. With
# `sound render on` the probe renders each tick's audio through the mixer
# (the backend playing), where it otherwise throws the queue away. `synth`
# switches as the AUDIO page does: the audio thread resets the backend asked
# for and replays the register shadow into it -- every register as last
# written, then a key-on for each channel whose keys were down -- so a note
# held across the switch keeps sounding. Twelve ticks after each switch (the
# cut clicks through the DC blocker for a few), the last four ticks still
# peak above -40 dBFS. Tick 420 of the title is a held chord: with the
# key-ons left out of the replay the route fails here at -48.6 dBFS; with
# them, -16.8. route_probe has no Q, so `synth q` falls back to the chip,
# reset and replayed again. Then the sequencer's writes since start-up,
# counted and hashed: the same as this route with its two `synth` lines
# taken out -- the switch never reaches the sequencer. docs/audio.md.
start new
sound render on
wait screen title
wait ticks 420
expect sound playing
synth chip
wait ticks 12
expect sound playing
synth q
wait ticks 12
expect sound playing
wait ticks 300
expect sound-writes 2143 $15673FE1
